      "text": [
        "517 - وَقَالَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: «مَنْ أُصِيبَ بِمُصِيبَةٍ جَزِعَ عَلَيْهَا أَوْ لَمْ يَجْزَعْ صَبَرَ عَلَيْهَا أَمْ لَمْ يَصْبِرْ كَانَ ثَوَابُهُ مِنَ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ اَلْجَنَّةَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.517 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) said:\n\"Whoever is afflicted with a calamity, whether they express intense grief over it or not, whether they exercise patience or not, their reward from Allah (swt), the Exalted and Glorious, is Paradise.\""
        ]
      }
